#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"This page explains the basic terms that appear everywhere in the web "
"interface and in the history, and where the values come from: **What is "
"measured and what does OpenEMS calculate?** This is particularly helpful "
"when values seem implausible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basic terms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Term\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| **Production** (generation)\n"
"| Electricity supplied by your own producers, usually the PV system. Includes AC producers (PV inverters, production meters) and DC producers (PV modules directly on the hybrid inverter).\n"
"| **Grid purchase** (buy)\n"
"| Electricity flowing from the public grid into the house.\n"
"| **Grid feed-in** (sell)\n"
"| Electricity flowing from the house into the public grid.\n"
"| **Charging**\n"
"| Electricity flowing into the home storage (battery).\n"
"| **Discharging**\n"
"| Electricity coming from the home storage.\n"
"| **Consumption**\n"
"| Electricity needed by all consumers in the house together: household, heat pump, wallbox, etc.\n"
"| **State of charge** (SoC)\n"
"| Charge level of the home storage in percent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Power and energy"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-power-and-energy
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Power** (watts, W / kW) is the instantaneous value: “3 kW are flowing "
"right now”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-power-and-energy
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Energy** (watt hours, Wh / kWh) is the amount over a period of time: “12 "
"kWh were purchased today”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-power-and-energy
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS stores energy as a running **meter reading**, like the electricity "
"meter in the basement. The energy of a day is the difference between the "
"meter readings (see xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[History])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Signs"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-signs
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "Some values have a sign that indicates the direction:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Value\n"
"| positive ({plus})\n"
"| negative (−)\n"
"\n"
"| Grid power\n"
"| Purchase from the grid\n"
"| Feed-in to the grid\n"
"| Storage power\n"
"| Discharging\n"
"| Charging\n"
"| Production, consumption\n"
"| always positive\n"
"| –\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The energy balance"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-energy-balance
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Everything that comes into the house must also go somewhere. This results in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consumption = production + grid purchase − grid feed-in + discharging − charging\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "or with signs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consumption = production + grid power + storage power\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Example: PV delivers 5 kW, the storage charges with 2 kW (−2 kW), 1 kW goes "
"into the grid (−1 kW). Consumption = 5 − 1 − 2 = 2 kW."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where the values come from"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is measured"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-is-measured
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "Measurements are only taken at a few points:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Measuring point\n"
"| delivers\n"
"\n"
"| **Grid meter** (at the house connection)\n"
"| Grid power per phase, meter readings for purchase and feed-in\n"
"| **Production meter** or PV inverter\n"
"| AC production per phase, production meter reading\n"
"| **Hybrid inverter** or DC charge controller\n"
"| DC production (PV directly on the storage system)\n"
"| **Storage system**\n"
"| Charging/discharging power, state of charge, capacity\n"
"| other meters (e.g. wallbox, heat pump)\n"
"| Power and energy of these individual consumers\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Important:** Whether a device measures its meter readings (energy) itself "
"or whether OpenEMS calculates them from the power depends on the device or "
"its connection. Many storage systems and some meters only supply power. "
"OpenEMS then counts up the energy itself. These self-counted values are "
"prone to jumps on restart (see xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[History])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is never measured: consumption"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-is-never-measured-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**The total consumption of the house is not measured in OpenEMS, but always "
"calculated**, according to the energy balance above:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consumption = grid power + AC production + AC power of the storage system\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Even an existing consumption meter is currently not used for this total."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"It follows that: **Any measurement error in grid, production or storage ends "
"up in consumption.** If, for example, a production meter is missing in the "
"configuration or the grid meter measures a phase incorrectly, the "
"consumption is wrong, in extreme cases even negative."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total values (_sum)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-total-values-sum
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS combines the values of all devices in the component `+_sum+`. The "
"web interface displays these values and they are stored in the history. They "
"are recalculated every second."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-total-values-sum
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "Explanation of the origin:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-total-values-sum
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Sum of the devices:** The values of all matching devices are added up. The "
"measurement therefore takes place in the device; OpenEMS only adds."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-total-values-sum
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Calculated:** The value is only created in `+_sum+` from other values. No "
"device measures it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Power values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Channel\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"| Origin\n"
"\n"
"| `+GridActivePower+` (and L1–L3)\n"
"| Grid power ({plus} purchase / − feed-in)\n"
"| Sum of the grid meters\n"
"| `+ProductionAcActivePower+` (and L1–L3)\n"
"| AC production\n"
"| Sum of the production meters / PV inverters\n"
"| `+ProductionDcActualPower+`\n"
"| DC production\n"
"| Sum of the DC charge controllers\n"
"| `+ProductionActivePower+`\n"
"| Total production\n"
"| calculated: AC {plus} DC\n"
"| `+EssActivePower+`\n"
"| Storage power at the inverter (AC; {plus} discharging / − charging)\n"
"| Sum of the storage systems\n"
"| `+EssActivePowerL1+`–`+L3+`\n"
"| Storage power per phase\n"
"| Sum; for storage systems without phase values **calculated** (total power ÷ 3)\n"
"| `+EssDischargePower+`\n"
"| Battery power ({plus} discharging / − charging); for hybrid systems on the battery side (DC)\n"
"| Sum of the storage systems\n"
"| `+EssSoc+`\n"
"| State of charge\n"
"| calculated: with several storage systems weighted by capacity; if a capacity is unknown, simple average\n"
"| `+ConsumptionActivePower+` (and L1–L3)\n"
"| Consumption\n"
"| **calculated:** grid {plus} AC production {plus} AC storage power\n"
"| `+UnmanagedConsumptionActivePower+`\n"
"| Consumption without controlled consumers (e.g. wallboxes)\n"
"| **calculated:** consumption − metered controlled consumers\n"
"| `+GridGensetActivePower+`\n"
"| Power of an emergency generator\n"
"| Sum of the corresponding meters\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Energy flows (“where does the electricity go?”)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-energy-flows-where-does-the-electricity-go
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"For the energy flow chart, OpenEMS divides the power values: how much solar "
"power goes into the house, how much into the storage, how much into the "
"grid? **These values are completely calculated**, there is no measurement "
"for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Channel\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| `+ProductionToConsumptionPower+`\n"
"| Solar → house\n"
"| `+ProductionToEssPower+`\n"
"| Solar → storage\n"
"| `+ProductionToGridPower+`\n"
"| Solar → grid\n"
"| `+GridToConsumptionPower+`\n"
"| Grid → house\n"
"| `+EssToConsumptionPower+`\n"
"| Storage → house\n"
"| `+GridToEssPower+`\n"
"| Grid → storage ({plus}) or storage → grid (−)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "The division follows fixed rules:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "If the storage is discharging, it supplies the house first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "If the storage is charging, the charge comes from production first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"The remaining production supplies the house; whatever is left goes into the "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "The grid covers the rest of the consumption."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "Any grid power still remaining is counted as grid ↔ storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Energy values (meter readings)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Channel\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"| Origin\n"
"\n"
"| `+GridBuyActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| Grid purchase\n"
"| Sum of the grid meters\n"
"| `+GridSellActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| Grid feed-in\n"
"| Sum of the grid meters\n"
"| `+ProductionAcActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| AC production\n"
"| Sum of the production meters\n"
"| `+ProductionDcActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| DC production\n"
"| Sum of the DC charge controllers\n"
"| `+ProductionActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| Total production\n"
"| calculated: AC {plus} DC\n"
"| `+EssActiveChargeEnergy+` / `+EssActiveDischargeEnergy+`\n"
"| Storage charging / discharging at the inverter (AC)\n"
"| Sum of the storage systems\n"
"| `+EssDcChargeEnergy+` / `+EssDcDischargeEnergy+`\n"
"| Charging / discharging on the battery side (for hybrid systems)\n"
"| Sum of the storage systems\n"
"| `+ConsumptionActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| Consumption\n"
"| **calculated:** (discharging {plus} purchase {plus} production) − (charging {plus} feed-in {plus} self-consumption of the producers)\n"
"| `+ProductionToConsumptionEnergy+`, `+ProductionToGridEnergy+`, `+ProductionToEssEnergy+`, `+GridToConsumptionEnergy+`, `+EssToConsumptionEnergy+`, `+GridToEssEnergy+`, `+EssToGridEnergy+`\n"
"| Energy flows\n"
"| **calculated:** counted up by OpenEMS from the calculated flow power values\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Note: For grid meters, the purchase is internally called “ProductionEnergy” "
"in OpenEMS and the feed-in “ConsumptionEnergy”, from the meter's point of "
"view. In `+_sum+` the names are unambiguous (Buy/Sell)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Channel\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"| Origin\n"
"\n"
"| `+GridMode+`\n"
"| Grid mode or island mode (emergency power)\n"
"| from the storage system\n"
"| `+GridBuyPrice+` / `+GridSellPrice+`\n"
"| Current purchase / feed-in price\n"
"| from the xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[tariff]\n"
"| `+EssCapacity+`\n"
"| Capacity of all storage systems\n"
"| Sum of the storage systems\n"
"| `+State+`\n"
"| Most severe current fault state of all components\n"
"| calculated\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "When consumption can become negative"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-consumption-can-become-negative
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Physically, a house cannot have negative consumption. However, because "
"consumption is **calculated** (grid {plus} AC production {plus} AC storage "
"power), negative values arise as soon as one of these values is missing, too "
"small or included with the wrong sign. Typical cases:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Case\n"
"| What happens\n"
"| Effect\n"
"\n"
"| **Producer missing in the configuration**\n"
"| A PV system feeds in but is not set up as a producer in OpenEMS. The grid meter sees the feed-in (negative), the production is missing from the calculation.\n"
"| Consumption too low; negative during feed-in\n"
"| **Measured value fails**\n"
"| A device temporarily does not supply a value, e.g. due to a communication fault. Missing values count as 0 in the total. If, for example, the PV inverter fails during feed-in, only the negative grid power remains.\n"
"| briefly or permanently negative\n"
"| **Wrong direction at the grid meter**\n"
"| Current transformer mounted the wrong way round, phases swapped or meter set incorrectly. Purchase and feed-in are (partly) measured swapped.\n"
"| Consumption too low or negative, often only on individual phases\n"
"| **Grid meter in the wrong place**\n"
"| The grid meter is located so that it does not capture part of the house, e.g. behind a sub-distribution board with PV feed-in.\n"
"| Balance is not correct, consumption wrong\n"
"| **Time offset between devices**\n"
"| The devices are queried one after the other; their values do not come from exactly the same moment. With rapid changes (cloud, wallbox switching, storage adjusting), the values do not match for seconds.\n"
"| brief negative peaks in the live view, usually without significance for the daily values\n"
"| **Self-consumption of the inverter**\n"
"| At night, a PV inverter draws a little power. A production meter then measures a small negative production.\n"
"| Consumption too low by this amount (usually only a few watts)\n"
"| **Storage power wrong**\n"
"| The storage system reports a wrong AC power or a wrong sign.\n"
"| Consumption wrong by this amount\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Negative consumption energy** in the history is also possible. In this "
"case, a meter reading of grid, production or storage has usually jumped "
"back, e.g. after a restart (see xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[History])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Procedure for negative consumption:** Look at grid power, production and "
"storage power individually. Does each value on its own match reality, e.g. "
"grid power compared with the electricity meter of the grid operator? If the "
"error only occurs on one phase, it is almost always due to a current "
"transformer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cascaded meters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does “cascaded” mean?"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-cascaded-mean
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Meters are **cascaded** (connected in series) if one meter is located behind "
"another in the electrical circuit. The front meter then **also** measures "
"the electricity flowing through the rear one."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grid ── Meter A ──┬── House consumption\n"
"                  └── Meter B ── PV system 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Meter A measures everything that flows through it, including the share of "
"meter B. Meter B only measures its branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "Typical examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid "a **sub-meter** in a sub-distribution board behind the grid meter,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"two PV systems whose **production meters** are in series (e.g. PV 2 is "
"connected via the line of PV 1),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"a PV inverter that is connected to OpenEMS **itself** and is additionally "
"measured via its own **production meter**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How OpenEMS adds up"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-adds-up
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS does not know how the meters are wired. It simply adds up **all "
"meters of one type**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Meter type (setting “Type”)\n"
"| is included in the total as\n"
"\n"
"| Grid (GRID)\n"
"| Grid power, purchase, feed-in\n"
"| Production (PRODUCTION); PV inverters automatically count as production\n"
"| Production\n"
"| Controlled consumer (MANAGED_CONSUMPTION_METERED), e.g. wallbox\n"
"| only for calculating consumption without controlled consumers\n"
"| Consumer (CONSUMPTION_METERED, CONSUMPTION_NOT_METERED)\n"
"| **not at all** (only displayed)\n"
"| Production and consumption (PRODUCTION_AND_CONSUMPTION)\n"
"| **not at all** (currently not taken into account in the total)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Effect on the total values"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-effect-on-the-total-values
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"If two meters **of the same type** are cascaded, the shared portion is "
"**counted twice**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Situation\n"
"| Consequence\n"
"\n"
"| Two production meters in series, or PV inverter plus production meter for the same system\n"
"| Production too high → consumption too high, energy flows wrong, self-consumption and self-sufficiency values too good\n"
"| Grid meter plus a sub-meter that is also set as grid\n"
"| Grid power, purchase and feed-in too high → consumption wrong, possibly negative during feed-in\n"
"| Sub-meter set as consumer\n"
"| no problem: consumer meters are not included in the total\n"
"| Wallbox meter as controlled consumer\n"
"| no problem for the total values; it is only subtracted from consumption to determine consumption without wallbox\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to avoid double counting"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-avoid-double-counting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Set **only one meter per energy flow** as grid or production. Set other "
"meters in the same branch as consumers (then they do not count) or omit them "
"in OpenEMS."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-avoid-double-counting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"A PV inverter that is directly connected does not need an additional "
"production meter, or vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-avoid-double-counting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Use **virtual meters**: With a “subtracting virtual meter” "
"(`+Meter.Virtual.Subtract+`) a branch can be calculated out, e.g. “meter A "
"minus meter B”. With an “adding virtual meter” (`+Meter.Virtual.Add+`) "
"several meters can be combined. Virtual meters have the setting “Add to "
"Sum”, which is **off** by default: they are then not included in the total "
"and do not change the total values. If “Add to Sum” is switched on, the "
"virtual meter counts in addition to the real meters. If it is to replace the "
"real meters in the total, these must not also be set as grid or production, "
"otherwise there is double counting again."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-avoid-double-counting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"Likewise, **storage clusters** (several storage systems combined into one) "
"are not counted additionally. Only the individual storage systems are "
"included in the total."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-avoid-double-counting
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/basics/energy-flows.adoc
msgid ""
"**Check:** Compare the production displayed by OpenEMS with the display of "
"the inverter or production meter. If it is significantly higher, go through "
"the points above. The equation “production = consumption {plus} feed-in” "
"does not help here: OpenEMS calculates the consumption itself from grid, "
"production and storage, so it always balances, even if there is double "
"counting."
msgstr ""

